+
+## Before you open a pull request
+Read CONTRIBUTING.md first. Its process rules apply to every change:
+- Open an issue first and wait for a maintainer to label it `status:accepted` before writing the patch (anything larger than a typo).
+- Keep one open pull request at a time until your first one is merged.
+- Tell the maintainers if you used an AI assistant; a person must have read the diff, run the tests and stand behind it.
+- Core ships primitives, not integrations: new tools and provider wrappers belong on the Hub.
+
+## Commands
+- Install: `pip install -e ".[dev]"`
+- Check: `make quality`; auto-fix style: `make style`
+- Test: `make test`
